<title>JAPAN: Toyota sees Japan vehicle sales up in '97.</title>
<headline>Toyota sees Japan vehicle sales up in '97.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Toyota Motor Corp president Hiroshi Okuda said on Monday he expects Japan's overall domestic vehicle sales, excluding 660cc minivehicles, to be about 5.4 million units in calendar 1997.</p>
<p>This would be up from a projected 5.3 million in 1996.</p>
<p>He gave his forecast during Toyota's year-end news conference in Nagoya, a company spokeswoman said.</p>
</text>
